title: '[pallet-revive] eth-rpc: decide reorgs by block canonicality, not by finalized
  height'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    ### Summary
    Adjust `update_latest` to distinguish a reconnect replay from a reorg by checking whether the cached best block is still canonical: a block with a lower number is accepted only when the cached block is no longer canonical. The check calls `chain_getBlockHash` and runs only for a lower-numbered block. The best block is also kept at or above the finalized block.

    - Keep the cached block when the lookup fails, so a failed request during a reconnect cannot move the head back.
    - Reject a best block below the finalized block.
    - Set the best block to the finalized block whenever the finalized number is at or above it.
    - Add unit tests for `SubxtBlockInfoProvider` using subxt's `MockRpcClient` (new `subxt-rpcs` dev-dependency).
crates:
- name: pallet-revive-eth-rpc
  bump: patch
